# Project 4 — Linux File Permissions

## Overview

This project focused on Linux file and directory permissions, ownership, and group-based access control. The lab was completed remotely from a 2015 MacBook Air to a Raspberry Pi 5 using SSH.

The goal was to gain hands-on experience managing Linux permissions and understanding how ownership, groups, and directory permissions control access to files.

## Devices Used

### Raspberry Pi 5
- Role: Linux server and cybersecurity home lab
- Operating System: Raspberry Pi OS
- Architecture: ARM64 / AArch64
- Hostname: raspberrypi
- Primary User: dedfr
- SSH Server: OpenSSH
- Project Directory: ~/permissions-lab

### 2015 MacBook Air
- Role: SSH client and remote administration workstation
- Operating System: macOS
- Used to remotely connect to and administer the Raspberry Pi 5
- SSH connection: ssh dedfr@10.0.0.98

